.TH AVR\-TESTS\-VIEW 1 "" "avr 0.4.1" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-tests-view \- Read the exact retained result, including available failure messages.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr tests view
[OPTIONS] TEST_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the exact retained result, including available failure messages.
.PP
An expired or unrecorded result is never replaced with a different capture. A recorded test failure is data, not a CLI error. No tests are rerun.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fITEST_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-capture\fR \fITEXT\fR
Exact capture from tests history. (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository (owner/name or rep-ID). Defaults to the git remote.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Defaults to the configured organization.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Occurrences to read (1-500). (default: 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-tests (1),
.BR avr-tests-captures (1),
.BR avr-tests-history (1),
.BR avr-tests-list (1),
.BR avr-tests-status (1)
